// `;` at the start of a line breaks the block: what follows is a new
// block, as after a blank line, with none needed. It works only at the start
// of a line, the way a list marker does.

// A line that follows is folded into the paragraph...
a
b

// ...unless it starts with `;`.
a
;b
c

// Elements side by side, one block each, with no blank line between them.
;@note(a)
;@note(b)
;@note(c)

// In the middle of a line, `;` is text. At the start of a line, `\;` is text.
a;b
c
\;d
